P(11,"We have now reached the evening that was to be known among them as the Night of Nights",
 "This is the evening of the Night of Nights. The boys eat their meal, and Peter has gone out to find the time.",
 "We have now reached the evening that was to be called the Night of Nights, because of its adventures and what came of them. The day had been almost quiet, as if it was quietly gathering its forces. Now the redskins in their blankets were at their posts above, and below the children were having their evening meal. Only Peter was missing. He had gone out to get the time. On the island, the way to get the time was to find the crocodile and stay near him until the clock struck.",
 ['upshot','posts'])
P(11,"None of them knew. Perhaps it was best not to know",
 "The children have one last happy hour. They sing, dance and have a pillow fight before the story.",
 "None of them knew. Maybe it was best not to know. Not knowing gave them one more happy hour. As it was to be their last hour on the island, let us be glad that there were sixty happy minutes in it. They sang and danced in their nightgowns. It was a deliciously creepy song, in which they pretended to be frightened of their own shadows. They hardly knew that soon shadows would close in on them, and they would shrink from them in real fear. The dance was so noisy and happy, and how they pushed and hit each other on the bed and off it! It was more a pillow fight than a dance. When it was finished, the pillows asked for one more round, like partners who know that they may never meet again. And the stories they told, before it was time for Wendy's good night story! Even Slightly tried to tell a story that night, but the beginning was so very dull that it shocked even him, and he said sadly:",
 ['rejoice','witting','buffeted','bout','uproariously','appalled'])
